# Project context: Red Team Control Center

Updated November 2, 2026. Current behavior is documented in README.md and
docs/README.md. This is a human-approved security assessment framework:
engagement review, policy-checked plans, individually approved execution,
analysis and immutable HTML reports. Autopilot drafts/proposes only.

## Source map

- frontend/src/App.jsx composes components and hooks; the UI is not a single-file application.
- backend/main.py and modules/workspace_api.py expose workflow and workspace routes.
- backend/models.py validates requests; database.py and migrations/ own persistence.
- modules/planner.py, exploit_planner.py and planners.py draft normal/campaign work.
- modules/policy_engine.py, scope_rules.py and command_values.py enforce restrictions.
- modules/jobs.py and worker.py own durable claims, recovery and cancellation.
- modules/executor.py and ssh_executor.py run local processes or trusted SSH/tmux commands.
- modules/evidence.py and secret_store.py protect originals; footholds.py ingests campaign evidence.
- modules/analyzer.py, verification.py and attack_paths.py analyze and correlate evidence.
- modules/workflow.py and report_versions.py coordinate revisions and immutable reports.
- modules/next_steps.py and auto_recommend.py create bounded advisory proposals.

See docs/api-reference.md for routes and docs/backend_technical_reference.md for
the full map, phase model and schema 0005_protected_workflows.

## Run and validate

Follow docs/deployment.md for Docker/native setup and docs/testing.md for isolated
test commands. Run frontend lint, tests and build after relevant UI changes.
Use temporary databases and encryption keys for backend regressions; do not run
live smoke/evaluation scripts as routine unit checks.

The November 2 record is 412 backend tests, later overlapping focused checks,
and 24 frontend tests. Counts are historical evidence, not a fixed invariant.
In PowerShell use Set-Location/Get-Content with -LiteralPath because this
repository directory contains brackets.

Native Uvicorn does not automatically load backend/.env or install scanners.
Provider/SSH secrets are configured in the application and encrypted at rest.
The API and workers must share the existing master key and data.
Public application probes are /health and /ready; FastAPI docs/schema are
also public. Other application routes use the operator API key.

## Workflow invariants

- Letter restrictions outrank operator edits and provider proposals. Require
  explicit approval and recheck scope, exclusions, time window, capabilities,
  phase prerequisites and command values when work starts.
- Normal phases are scoping, recon, vuln_analysis, exploitation,
  post_exploitation and reporting. Aggressive lab mode adds
  credential_validation, lateral_movement and impact.
- Freeze executed step index/tool/command/phase/enabled state. Keep idle,
  unexecuted steps editable; do not freeze the entire plan after one execution.
- Invalidate the earliest execution-bearing changed phase and its dependents.
  Preserve earlier findings. No-op saves preserve reports; reason-only edits
  preserve analysis but invalidate current reporting.
- Use plan versions for operator edits and workflow revision claims for mutations
  and slow publication. Helpers flush within caller-owned transactions.
- Analysis/verification/ingestion/phase advancement/eligible drafting commit
  together. Autopilot local changes are atomic; advisory work checks revision
  after its separate provider call.
- Stage reports uniquely and publish a committed immutable version pointer.
  Never overwrite report_<id>.html as the current-report contract.
- Promotion requires owned evidence, parent host-wide permission and no exclusion
  overlap. Retain restrictions; do not widen URL/path/port-only permission.
- External workers wait for both schema head and protected-evidence backfill.
  Deletion honors campaign dependencies; parents with children return conflict.

## Evidence and execution guardrails

- Preserve encrypted raw command/stdout/stderr and independent attempt archives.
  Public/live/provider/report text uses redacted projections and original hashes.
- Use $$loot:<id>$$ references for recovered credentials. Plan source is executable
  text, not a general secret vault; redaction is not a universal secret detector.
- Original reveals commit evidence_access audits before returning no-store
  responses. Strict original decryption must fail on unreadable data.
- Live output exposes complete redacted lines only. Preserve table context in
  the bounded private buffer; never leak chunk-split or truncated secrets.
- SSH arguments must retain literal local-executor semantics. Inspect and
  independently trust the host fingerprint before saving it. No silent local fallback.
- The shared SSH tmux lock is process-local; it does not coordinate separate workers.
- A failed scanner is not a clean target. ZAP baseline exits 1/2 are findings.
  Banners, HTTP 200 and AI prose do not establish verified exploitation.

## Parser and policy regressions to preserve

- Engagement parsing handles PDF DEL (\\x7f) bullets. Excluded addresses must
  not become inferred targets.
- Do not double-prefix URL schemes or pass host:port to host-only DNS/Nmap tools.
- CIDR authorization checks subnet containment, not just the base address.
  Nmap sweep findings retain host-qualified endpoints before deduplication.
- Strip ANSI escapes before deterministic parsing. Nuclei accepts its optional
  protocol field and case-normalizes severity; info maps to Low.
- Curl header findings require an actual HTTP status. Tentative Nmap services
  remain findings with appropriate confidence.
- Keep Nuclei 3.11.1 or validate any replacement; an older version crashed with
  concurrent map writes. Seed templates in the image and disable runtime updates.
- The 360-second timeout followed an observed approximately 308-second Nuclei run
  at the approved rate. Re-measure before adjusting time or rate bounds.
- Next-step dedupe allows materially different flags for the same tool/host;
  do not suppress legitimate deepening using only tool plus host.
- Independent sqlmap verification must match category, endpoint and parameter,
  reject failed/ambiguous/secondary-URL evidence, and preserve path/query identity.

## UI regressions to preserve

- Scope asynchronous responses to the selected assessment and credential
  generation. Stale 401s must not invalidate a newly entered key.
- Background refresh preserves unsaved plan/settings edits. Failed navigation
  keeps the current assessment usable; creation handles unsaved edits explicitly.
- Use the shared request helper for uploads, friendly errors and cancellation.
  Clear the file input after selection so choosing the same file triggers again.
- Report generation provides explicit open/download links; avoid popup dependence.
  Refresh history after regeneration even if assessment status stays reported.
- Retired legacy reports explain regeneration and restricted original access.
  Recorded/live output clearly represents redacted evidence.
- Keep busy/duplicate-action guards, accessible focus/keyboard controls, mobile
  navigation and reduced-motion support.

## Demo preparation

Use reviewed, current engagement dates and authorized targets. Follow
docs/deployment.md for local or SSH execution; do not reset volumes just to start
a demo. Rehearse import, plan review, approval, execution, analysis and reporting.
Workflow-only smoke, mocked browser fixtures and unit tests do not prove live
scanner/provider/VM compatibility. Historical letters and audit records are
examples, not continuing authorization for a target.
